  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>rezafungin_acetate</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>J02AX08</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>one compartment, IV dosing <small>(PK_1C)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Roepcke S et al. 2023</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>healthy volunteers and patients with candidemia/invasive candidiasis</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>rezafungin</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>accepted with caveats</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_rezafungin_acetate/RezafunginAcetate_Roepcke2023_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>CL</td><td>2.77</td><td>L/h</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>theta_cl_category</td><td>9.25</td><td></td><td><small>equation variable</small></td></tr><tr><td>V1</td><td>3.96</td><td>L</td><td><small>V</small></td></tr><tr><td>Q2</td><td>5.38</td><td>L/h</td><td><small>Q</small></td></tr><tr><td>Q3</td><td>4.37</td><td>L/h</td><td><small>Q3</small></td></tr><tr><td>theta_q319_weight_power</td><td>16.4</td><td></td><td><small>equation variable</small></td></tr><tr><td>theta_q319_weight_power</td><td>9.47</td><td></td><td><small>equation variable</small></td></tr><tr><td>theta_v1_category</td><td>18.1</td><td></td><td><small>equation variable</small></td></tr><tr><td>theta_q319_weight_power</td><td>11.4</td><td></td><td><small>equation variable</small></td></tr><tr><td>theta_q319_weight_power</td><td>14.9</td><td></td><td><small>equation variable</small></td></tr></table><h4>About rezafungin_acetate</h4><p>Rezafungin acetate is an antifungal medicine used to treat invasive candida infections of the bloodstream. It is a newer antifungal that has been authorised in the United States but is not approved in the European Union.</p><p><small><b>Unverified</b> — written by glm-5.3-flash from general knowledge (no Wikidata entry found) and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Roepcke S et al. (2023). Population pharmacokinetic modeling and target attainment analyses of rezafungin for the treatment of candidemia and invasive candidiasis. <i>Antimicrobial agents and chemotherapy 67(12):e0091623</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1128/aac.00916-23\">10.1128/aac.00916-23</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38014945\">38014945</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Roepcke_2023: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"),
